cctext patch 0004: match font-family names case-insensitively.

plutovg's face cache compares family names with strcmp, so "arial" and
"Arial" were different families and SVGs from different tools fell back
inconsistently. CSS matches family names ASCII case-insensitively; the
lookup key is now lowercased and cctext-render registers its bundled
faces (and their aliases: sans-serif, Arial, Helvetica, ...) under
lowercase names. No system fonts are loaded (LUNASVG_DISABLE_LOAD_SYSTEM_FONTS).

Apply after 0003.

--- a/source/svglayoutstate.cpp
+++ b/source/svglayoutstate.cpp
@@ -594,6 +594,12 @@ Font SVGLayoutState::font() const
         }
 
         std::string font_family(family);
+        // cctext patch: family names match ASCII case-insensitively (CSS
+        // Fonts 4, 5.1); the host registers its faces under lowercase names.
+        for(auto& ch : font_family) {
+            if(ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z')
+                ch = static_cast<char>(ch - 'A' + 'a');
+        }
         if(!font_family.empty()) {
             face = fontFaceCache()->getFontFace(font_family, bold, italic);
         }
